# SYNTHETIC FORTINET FORTIGATE SYSLOG TEST DATA (key=value format) - NOT REAL PRODUCTION LOGS
# FOR SYSLOG LENS TESTING ONLY. Fake device IDs; RFC 5737/1918 addresses only.
# Format: <PRI>date=YYYY-MM-DD time=HH:MM:SS[ tz="+HHMM"] devname="..." devid="..." logid="..." type="..." subtype="..." level="..." ... msg="..."
# date=/time= are the FortiGate's own DEVICE-LOCAL time, not UTC. Timestamp preference order
# (see fortiTime() in syslog-lens.html): (a) eventtime= epoch, unit by digit count (10=s,
# 13=ms, 16=us, 19=ns); (b) date=+time= combined with tz=; (c) date=+time= with no tz=, read as
# the viewer's own local time. The lines below deliberately exercise all three paths, including
# two tz= spellings ("+0800" and "+08:00") and a negative offset ("-0500"), plus a same-instant
# pair (one via eventtime=, one via date=+time=+tz=) to prove the two paths agree.
